---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, PUSH_RELAY } from '../../data';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  description="Arkhe collects no data. It talks to the IRC servers and bouncers you configure; optional push notifications pass through a content-blind relay."
>
  <h1 class="mt-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="!mt-2 text-sm text-ink-400">Arkhe for iPhone &amp; iPad · Last updated: October 11, 2026</p>

  <p>
    Arkhe ("the app") is an IRC client. It connects to IRC servers and bouncers that <em>you</em>
    choose. There are no Arkhe accounts, no analytics, no advertising SDKs and no telemetry of
    any kind.
  </p>

  <div class="card mt-8 !p-6">
    <p class="!mt-0"><strong>Short version:</strong> we do not collect, store, sell or share your
    personal data. Your settings and recent history stay on your device, and your conversations
    go directly to the servers you configure. The one service we run, the optional push relay,
    only ever sees encrypted notifications it cannot read.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <p>The app stores the following locally, in its own sandbox and in the iOS Keychain:</p>
  <table class="mt-4">
    <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Server and bouncer settings, nicknames and app preferences</td><td>App storage</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Passwords, SASL credentials, client-certificate passphrases and an optional uploader token</td><td>iOS Keychain (encrypted)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Recent conversation history (the last 500 lines per conversation), so chats open instantly. You can turn this off in Settings, which deletes it</td><td>App storage</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The encryption keys used to decrypt push notifications</td><td>iOS Keychain, shared with the app’s notification extension</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>All of this is removed when you delete the app.</p>

  <h2>What the app connects to</h2>
  <p><strong>The IRC servers and bouncers you configure.</strong> Your nickname, messages and
  connection details go directly to them. They are run by third parties (or by you) and are
  governed by their own policies, not this one. We have no access to those connections.</p>

  <p><strong>File uploads, only when you attach something.</strong> If your server offers a file
  host, the file is uploaded there, signed in with your server login. Otherwise it goes to the
  custom uploader you configured. We do not operate either and never receive your files.</p>

  <p><strong>Images and link previews.</strong> When <em>Load images &amp; link previews</em> is
  on (Settings → Media), the app fetches images and page previews for links posted in your
  conversations. Like opening any link, this reveals your IP address to the site hosting them.
  Turn it off to only fetch content when you tap a link.</p>

  <p><strong>Push notifications, optional and off by default.</strong> If you turn on
  <em>Push when app is closed</em>, your bouncer encrypts each notification for your device
  (Web Push, RFC 8291) and sends it to our relay at <code>{PUSH_RELAY}</code>, which forwards it to
  Apple’s Push Notification service. The relay sees only the encrypted payload, your device’s
  push token and the address of your bouncer. It cannot read the notifications, keeps no
  access logs and stores nothing. Delivery through Apple is governed by Apple’s privacy policy.
  You can point the app at a relay you run yourself.</p>

  <p>The app contacts no other services: no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising
  networks.</p>

  <h2>Data sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, share or disclose your data, because we do not collect it.</p>

  <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>Arkhe is not directed at children and does not collect personal information from anyone.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the app’s data practices change, we will update this page and the date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Write to <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
